       <item>
        <TDFORMAT>AS</TDFORMAT>
        <TDLINE>The /CTDI/CL_PRINT_DRIVER_TEMPLATE class is a reference subclass layout</TDLINE>
       </item>
       <item>
        <TDFORMAT></TDFORMAT>
        <TDLINE> template. It serves as a blueprint for developers implementing new</TDLINE>
       </item>
       <item>
        <TDFORMAT></TDFORMAT>
        <TDLINE> print driver subclasses in the dynamic framework.</TDLINE>
       </item>
       <item>
        <TDFORMAT>U1</TDFORMAT>
        <TDLINE>USAGE DETAILS</TDLINE>
       </item>
       <item>
        <TDFORMAT>AS</TDFORMAT>
        <TDLINE>Developers can copy this class or study its hook redefinitions to:</TDLINE>
       </item>
       <item>
        <TDFORMAT>B1</TDFORMAT>
        <TDLINE>- unpack_io_data: Read custom parameters from execution context.</TDLINE>
       </item>
       <item>
        <TDFORMAT>B1</TDFORMAT>
        <TDLINE>- fetch_data_from_db: Perform database selections or call data</TDLINE>
       </item>
       <item>
        <TDFORMAT></TDFORMAT>
        <TDLINE>  provider classes.</TDLINE>
       </item>
       <item>
        <TDFORMAT>B1</TDFORMAT>
        <TDLINE>- map_and_register_data: Map customized fields and register them</TDLINE>
       </item>
       <item>
        <TDFORMAT></TDFORMAT>
        <TDLINE>  safely for Smart Forms and Adobe Forms rendering.</TDLINE>
       </item>
      </LINES>
